              "text": "To log into your Microsoft OneDrive account, choose the option below that fits your current device:\n\n### 1. On a Web Browser (Computer or Mobile)\n1. Go directly to the official **[OneDrive Sign-in Page](https://onedrive.live.com)**.\n2. Enter the **email address, phone number, or Skype name** associated with your Microsoft account and click **Next**.\n3. Enter your **password** and click **Sign in**. \n   * *If you have two-step verification enabled, you will be prompted to enter a code sent to your phone or authenticator app.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. On a Windows PC\nOneDrive comes pre-installed on Windows 10 and Windows 11:\n1. Click the **Start menu** (or press the Windows key), search for **\"OneDrive\"**, and open the app.\n2. Enter your Microsoft account email address and click **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your password and follow the brief onboarding setup prompts to select which folders you want to sync to your PC.\n\n---\n\n### 3. On a Mac\n1. Open the **OneDrive app** (if you don't have it, you can download it from the Mac App Store).\n2. Launch OneDrive via **Finder** > **Applications** or search for it using **Spotlight** (Cmd + Space).\n3. Enter your Microsoft credentials to log in and set up your synced folder.\n\n---\n\n### 4. On a Mobile Device (iPhone, iPad, or Android)\n1. Download the free **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the **Apple App Store** or **Google Play Store**.\n2. Open the app and tap **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your Microsoft account credentials to access your stored files, photos, and documents.\n\n---\n\n### Troubleshooting Login Issues\n* **Forgot your password?** Click the **\"Forgot password?\"** link on the login page, or go directly to the **[Microsoft Password Reset Page](https://account.live.com/ResetPassword.aspx)** to recover your account.\n* **Using a school or work account?** If your email is provided by your organization, make sure to select \"Work or school account\" if prompted, as your login page might be redirected to your organization's specific portal.",
